timestamp=2026-07-14T14:00:25.516Z level=INFO run=fa17918a message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/proof_analysis.txt\nKey observations:\n1. leads_to(q) = always(p.implies(eventually(q)))\n2. leads_to(always(q)) = always(p.implies(eventually(always(q))))\n3. We need: if q holds at some point, and q.and(next).implies(later(q)) always holds, \n   and next always holds, then q holds forever from that point.\n\nHelper: q_stable_from(ex, i) where q holds at i and next holds everywhere\n  -> q holds at i+k for all k\n\nMain proof:\n- Take any ex satisfying spec\n- spec.entails(p.leads_to(always(q))) means:\n  forall ex, spec.satisfied_by(ex) => (p.leads_to(always(q))).satisfied_by(ex)\n- p.leads_to(always(q)) = always(p.implies(eventually(always(q))))\n  = forall i, (p.implies(eventually(always(q)))).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i))\n- So for any i, if p.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i)), then eventually(always(q)).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i))\n- From p.leads_to(q) and i, we get j s.t. q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i).suffix(j))\n- i.e., q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i+j))\n- Then always(q).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i+j)) by stability\n- Then eventually(always(q)).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(i))\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-07-14T14:00:25.516Z level=INFO run=fa17918a message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat /tmp/proof_analysis.txt" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
