timestamp=2026-07-14T14:01:14.962Z level=INFO run=fa17918a message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/analysis2.txt\nq.and(next).implies(later(q)).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))\n= (q.and(next)).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) ==> later(q).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))\n= (q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) && next.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))) ==> later(q).satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))\n= (q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) && next.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))) ==> q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx).suffix(1))\n= (q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) && next.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))) ==> q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx+1))\n\nSo: forall idx, (q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) && next.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx))) ==> q.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx+1))\n\nBut next_preserves_inv_rec requires:\nforall |idx| inv.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) && next.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx)) ==> inv.satisfied_by(ex.suffix(idx + 1))\n\nNote: ex.suffix(idx).suffix(1) vs ex.suffix(idx + 1) -- these should be equal\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
